tanding of a specific subject or explore new areas of interest.\n\n4. Professional network expansion: Going back to school presents the opportunity to connect with like-minded individuals, build new relationships, and expand one's professional network. This could increase future job opportunities and lay the foundation for long-lasting personal and professional connections that would help individuals succeed in their chosen careers.\n\n5. Personal resilience and adaptation: In recent years, lifelong learning has become increasingly essential given the rapidly changing job market and economy. Some people may decide to return to school to retrain themselves and stay relevant in their career, demonstrating their ability to adapt and maintain a growth mindset.\n\nIn conclusion, \"better themselves\" appeals to human common sense because it encompasses a wide range of motivations that guide individuals in their pursuit of personal and professional growth. This intrinsic desire to improve one's standing in life, either through career advancements or intellectual achievements, is a core aspect of the human experience. Going back to school serves as a testament to an individual's dedication to self-improvement and their commitment to attaining the knowledge, skills, and connections required to thrive in today's world."}]}
