{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "What type of details about tokugawa ieshige  can be gathered from the following bio?  Bio: tokugawa ieshige ; 徳川 家重 -lrb- january 28 , 1712 -- july 13 , 1761 -rrb- was the ninth shogun of the tokugawa shogunate of japan . the first son of tokugawa yoshimune , his mother was the daughter of Ōkubo tadanao , known as osuma no kata . his childhood name was nagatomi-maru . he underwent the `` genpuku '' coming-of-age ceremony in 1725 . his first wife , nami-no-miya , was the daughter of prince fushimi-no-miya kuninaga -lrb- 伏見宮 邦永親王 -rrb- . his second wife , okō , was the daughter of one of the courtiers who had followed his high-born first wife from the imperial court to the shogunal court in edo . this famously good-natured second wife was the mother of ieharu , who would become ieshige 's heir . in `` enkyō '' 2 , ieshige was made shogun . ieshige suffered from chronic ill health and a severe speech defect . yoshimune 's choice of ieshige as his heir created considerable controversy within the shogunate as his younger brothers tokugawa munetake and tokugawa munetada appeared to be far more suitable candidates . yoshimune continued to insist on his decision , favoring the confucian principle of primogeniture ; and ieshige continued in the role of formal head of the shogunate . yoshimune directed affairs after his official retirement in 1745 . this attention was designed to ensure that ieshige was secure in his office . ieshige remained shogun until 1760 . uninterested in government affairs , ieshige left all decisions in the hands of his chamberlain , Ōoka tadamitsu -lrb- 1709 -- 1760 -rrb- . he officially retired in 1760 and assumed the title of '' Ōgosho , '' appointed his first son tokugawa ieharu as the 10th shogun , and died the following year . ieshige 's second son tokugawa shigeyoshi became the founder of the shimizu tokugawa clan , which together with the tayasu and hitotsubashi -lrb- established by ieshige 's younger brothers -rrb- became the `` gosankyō '' , three cadet branches of the tokugawa family from which future shoguns might be selected if the main line were to die out . they joined...\nA:"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "From the bio, we can gather the following details about Tokugawa Ieshige:\n\n1. He was born on January 28, 1712, and died on July 13, 1761.\n2. Ieshige was the ninth shogun of the Tokugawa shogunate of Japan.\n3. He was the first son of Tokugawa Yoshimune, and his mother was the daughter of Ōkubo Tadanao named Osuma no Kata.\n4. His childhood name was Nagatomi-maru.\n5. He underwent the genpuku coming-of-age ceremony in 1725.\n6. Ieshige had two wives: Nami-no-Miya, daughter of Prince Fushimi-no-Miya Kuninaga, and Okō, daughter of a courtier who followed Nami-no-Miya.\n7. Okō, his second wife, was the mother of Ieharu, who became Ieshige's heir.\n8. Ieshige was made shogun in Enkyō 2 (around 1744).\n9. He suffered from chronic ill health and a severe speech defect.\n10. His appointment as shogun was controversial, as his younger brothers seemed more suitable for the position.\n11. His father, Yoshimune, insisted on Ieshige's appointment and continued to direct shogunate affairs even after retirement in 1745.\n12. Ieshige remained shogun until 1760 but was uninterested in governing, leaving decisions to his chamberlain, Ōoka Tadamitsu.\n13. He retired in 1760 and appointed his first son, Tokugawa Ieharu, as the 10th shogun.\n14. His second son, Tokugawa Shigeyoshi, became the founder of the Shimizu Tokugawa clan, part of the \"Gosankyō\" cadet branches of the Tokugawa family."}]}
