{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a teacher. Given a task, you explain in simple steps what the task is asking, any guidelines it provides and how to use those guidelines to find the answer."}, {"role": "user", "content": "In this task, you're given an article, a question which often contains a blank, four options (associated with \"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\") and the answer to that question. Your task is to classify whether the given answer is correct or not by providing \"Yes\" or \"No\", based on the article.\nQ: Article: Have you ever been to a wedding and simply loved the bride's bouquet ?More than likely some part of it was the Hawaiian Wedding Plant. This foreign houseplant can be enjoyed by anyone, not just brides. With a little proper attention and careful planning on location, this foreign houseplant, which is from Madagascar, can be brought into the home where it can become an interesting focus. Caring for the Hawaiian Wedding Plant is not much different from caring for any other houseplants that may already be in your home. The only difference between this type of houseplant and others is the amount of the basic requirements that this foreign houseplant needs to survive and perform beautifully. During the growing season, this plant requires its wet soil, but when winter rolls around, this plant needs its soil to be kept drier. Hawaiian Wedding Plants should also be potted in well-drained soil and placed in a location that receives full sun. That the soil must be kept wet does not mean that it should sit in water, so the soil must drain easily or this plant will not survive. Water the plant daily and feed this plant every two to three weeks with a little fertilizer  for acid-loving plants. Prune in early spring, even as early as February. If these needs are met, this plant will stay beautiful. The most special feature of this foreign houseplant is its long lasting blooms combined with its unbelievable sweet smell. The Hawaiian Wedding Plant blooms the heaviest in the spring months, but has been known to bloom in any warm months, so do not be surprised to find blooms most time of the year except maybe _ \n Question: The Hawaiian Wedding Plant comes from  _  . \n Options: (A) Hawaii (B) China (C) Madagascar (D) Alaska \n Asnwer: C\nA:"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "In this task, you are asked to determine if the given answer is correct or not based on the information provided in the article.\n\n1. Read the article to understand its content and context.\n2. Look at the question and identify the key information needed to answer it. In this case, the question asks, \"The Hawaiian Wedding Plant comes from _.\"\n3. Review the article to find any information related to the origin or location of the Hawaiian Wedding Plant. The relevant information in the article is, \"this foreign houseplant, which is from Madagascar.\"\n4. Using the found information, examine the options provided (A-Hawaii, B-China, C-Madagascar, D-Alaska).\n5. Compare the information from the article with the given answer: Answer C (Madagascar).\n6. Determine if the given answer corresponds to the information in the article. In this case, the answer is correct as the article states that the Hawaiian Wedding Plant comes from Madagascar.\n7. Provide the response \"Yes\" if the given answer is correct or \"No\" if it is incorrect. In this case, your response should be \"Yes.\""}]}
