ney Houston -- Family Told She Died from Rx NOT Drowning \n  \n Whitney Houston Cause Of Death -- Family Told She Died From Prescription Drugs, Not Drowning \n  \n 's family was told by L.A. County Coroner officials ... the singer did not die from drowning, but rather from what appears to be a combination of Xanax and other prescription drugs mixed with alcohol ... this according to family sources.We're told Coroner's officials informed the family there was not enough water in Whitney's lungs to lead to the conclusion that she drowned.Our sources say the family was told Whitney may well have died before her head became submerged.And family sources tell us ... it was actually Whitney's aunt,, who discovered Whitney's body in the bathtub. Mary had laid out Whitney's dress for the evening on the bed and then left for about a half hour. When Whitney didn't come out of the bathroom, Mary entered, pulled Whitney out of the tub and began administering CPR.And we're told ... Whitney's mom has arranged to have the singer's body flown back to Atlanta, as early as tomorrow. The family was told the Coroner has no problem releasing the body because there is no evidence of foul play -- and unless cops put a hold on the body, it can be flown back East. |||||"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Singer Whitney Houston was found dead at the age of 48 in her hotel room at the Beverly Hilton. The body was discovered in the bathtub, with no visible signs of trauma. Los Angeles Coroner Assistant Chief Ed Winter stated that additional testing was required to determine the cause of death, and it may take six to eight weeks for the results to be available.\n\nIt was revealed through an autopsy that there was water in Whitney Houston's lungs at the time of her death. However, the exact amount of water needs to be determined before a ruling on whether her death was a result of drowning. Authorities are also considering the possibility that Whitney Houston may have been dead before she went underwater. Toxicology results will be expected to come back in 4-6 weeks.\n\nWhitney Houston's family was informed by L.A. County Coroner officials that her death was not due to drowning, but rather a likely combination of prescription drugs, like Xanax, mixed with alcohol. There was not enough water in her lungs to confirm that she drowned. It is suggested that Houston may have died before her head was submerged in the water. Her body was discovered by her aunt, who started administering CPR after pulling her out of the tub.\n\nWhitney Houston's mother later arranged for her body to be flown back to Atlanta, with the Coroner's approval since there was no evidence of foul play."}]}
