s cities became more crowded, bones were sometimes recovered after a period, and placed in ossuaries where they might be arranged for artistic effect, as at the Capuchin Crypt in Rome or the Czech Sedlec Ossuary, which has a chandelier made of skulls and bones., can you guess it ?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Yes, based on the provided information, the answer to the question \"What shows a Christian iconography emerging, initially from Roman popular decorative art?\" is found in the statement, \"The Catacombs of Rome contain most of the surviving Christian art of the Early Christian period, mainly in the form of frescos and sculpted sarcophagi.\" These catacombs show a Christian iconography emerging, initially from Roman popular decorative art, but later borrowing from official imperial and pagan motifs."}]}
