guish between natural and human-induced seismic activity.\n\n5. Finally, the occurrence of earthquakes is inherently probabilistic, meaning that even with advanced monitoring and prediction techniques, there is always an element of uncertainty involved. This makes it impossible to predict the exact time and location of the next major earthquake with absolute certainty.\n\nIn conclusion, due to the complex nature of the Earth's crust, the influence of various factors on seismic activity, and the inherent uncertainty involved in predicting earthquakes, it is not possible to tell the exact time and location of the next major earthquake."}]}
