e of the Great Salt Lake. The highest elevation is Flat Top Mountain (Utah) at 10,620 ft (3,237 m). The name Oquirrh was taken from the Goshute word meaning \"wood sitting.\"   - Temple Square is a complex, owned by The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints (LDS Church), in the center of Salt Lake City, Utah. In recent years, the usage of the name has gradually changed to include several other church facilities that are immediately adjacent to Temple Square. Contained within Temple Square are the Salt Lake Temple, Salt Lake Tabernacle, Salt Lake Assembly Hall, the Seagull Monument, and two visitors' centers.    What is the relationship between 'kbzn' and 'ogden'?\nA:"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "KBZN, now known as 97.9 FM, is a Hot Adult Contemporary music-formatted radio station broadcasting to the Salt Lake City metropolitan area, which includes the city of Ogden. Both Salt Lake City and Ogden are part of the Salt Lake City-Ogden-Provo Combined Statistical Area, a corridor of contiguous urban and suburban development stretched along the Wasatch Front. In summary, the relationship between KBZN and Ogden is that KBZN serves as a radio station broadcasting to the larger area, which includes Ogden as one of the cities in its coverage area."}]}
