ynthetic process.\n\nOther pigments exist in plants as well, such as carotenoids and anthocyanins, which assist in light harvesting and provide photoprotection during periods of excessive light exposure. These pigments are also complex molecules that contribute to the overall process of light absorption by plants.\n\nConsidering the complexity of chlorophyll and other pigments involved in light absorption, it can be concluded that among the provided answer choices, \"complex\" is the most appropriate description for the molecules used by plants to absorb light energy."}]}
