til the age of seven or eight, play and work mean much the same to a child.But once reading has been mastered, then books and school become the main source of learning.Toys are still interesting and valuable, which lead up to new hobbies, but their significance has changed --to a child of nine or ten years old, toys and games mean, as to adults, relaxation and fun. Question: 62. The passage tells us that children are the most curious when they are about  _  . Answer:\nThe answer is:"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "three to five years old"}]}
