verse and inclusive history allows everyone to understand the contributions of various groups in context, and promotes a more accurate understanding of history.\n- Honest dialogue must go beyond black and white and be inclusive of all races and ethnicities, with all parties willing to be critiqued as well as offer criticism.\n- Holder's statements on America's need to confront its racial history and engage in cross-racial dialogue have already sparked important conversations, showing progress."}]}
